    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "First introduce a pronumeral and then solve the equation.\n\nA boy throws away one-third of the cakes he has cooked. If he has 34 left, how many did he cook in the first place?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "51 cakes.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the number of cakes he cooked. The fraction remaining is $1-\\frac13=\\frac23$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2x}{3}&=34\\\\2x&=102\\\\x&=51\\end{align*}$$\nHe cooked 51 cakes.\n\nCheck: $51-\\frac13\\times51=51-17=34$ cakes remain.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
